From: v5 schema-evolution plan M13 (T4c)
Subject: [PATCH] bank-sync: stamp BalanceSyncState snapshots with the state-shape version

Apply AFTER the next go-cqrs-lite tag wave ships decider/v4 > v4.7.2 and
snapshot/v4 > v4.6.2 (bank-sync builds hermetically via buildGoModule +
vendorHash — dev-time sibling replaces would break the nix build, so this
patch waits for the proxy tags). Then: `go get` both pins, `go mod tidy`,
apply, run the battery.

The declared version is "1" because BalanceSyncState's shape has never
changed: the stamp's value is the NEXT shape change, which then only bumps
this constant instead of shipping silently-stale snapshots.

diff --git a/internal/cqrs/infrastructure.go b/internal/cqrs/infrastructure.go
--- a/internal/cqrs/infrastructure.go
+++ b/internal/cqrs/infrastructure.go
@@ -379,6 +379,12 @@ func SetupInfrastructure(
 	upcastingStore := event.DecorateStore(adapter, nil, upcastingChain.SourceTransform())

+	// balanceSyncStateShape stamps every snapshot with the shape version of
+	// BalanceSyncState (T4 shape guard): a future State shape change bumps
+	// this constant and stale snapshots are discarded + rebuilt from the
+	// journal instead of decoded into the new shape. "1" is the first stamp —
+	// the shape has never changed; see decider.WithSnapshotStateVersion.
+	const balanceSyncStateShape = "1"
+
 	deciderRepo, err := decider.NewRepository(
 		upcastingStore, bus, balanceSyncDecider,
 		decider.WithSnapshotStore[BalanceSyncState](countingSnapshotStore),
 		decider.WithCodec[BalanceSyncState](snapshotCodec),
+		decider.WithSnapshotStateVersion[BalanceSyncState](balanceSyncStateShape),
 		decider.WithSnapshotStrategy[BalanceSyncState](snapshotStrategy),
 		decider.WithEnricher[BalanceSyncState](event.CompositeEnricher(
 			event.CommandCausalityEnricher,
